INT. LAUNDROMAT - NIGHT

Closed. Fluorescent hum. Dryers dark. One machine on the end, still ticking as it cools.

An answering machine on the counter. Red light blinking.

Keys in the lock. The door swings.

ILSE, 60, enters in a rain slicker. Hair flat. Laundry basket on her hip. Empty.

She sets it down. Presses play.

ILSE (V.O.)
(recorded, cheerful)
You've reached Sunshine Wash and Fold. We can't come to the phone.

Ilse stares at the machine.

ILSE (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recorded)
Leave a message. Or just bring your socks!

A man's laugh, behind the recording. Cut off.

She presses stop. Presses play. The laugh again.

Stop. Play. Stop.

She lifts the machine. Holds it overhead. Her arms shake.

She sets it down. Softly. Presses play.

ILSE (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recorded)
Or just bring your socks!

Ilse sits on the folding table. Folds her hands. Listens to it all the way through, twice.
